## **16. Technical performance and security**

The game must be optimized for the target platform.

- Use level-of-detail systems for distant objects.
- Implement occlusion culling.
- Optimize textures and 3D models.
- Use object pooling for zombies and projectiles.
- Limit active zombie AI based on distance.
- Use navigation meshes for intelligent movement.
- Use asynchronous asset loading.
- Optimize lighting and shadows.
- Support configurable graphics quality.
- Prevent frame-rate drops during large zombie hordes.
- Use secure authentication tokens.
- Validate inventory and transactions server-side.
- Protect cloud saves from unauthorized modifications.
- Include recovery procedures for interrupted saving.

Do not generate an enormous world with every building and zombie loaded simultaneously. Stream world regions and activate AI according to player proximity.

