# **19. My additional recommendations**

There are three features I would particularly encourage adding to make this game stand out.

[“Story Exploration: Surviving the Scorched Earth Social, Economic, and Cultural Dynamics in a Post-Apocalyptic World” | by Simonimpey | Feb, 2026 | Medium](https://images.openai.com/static-rsc-4/F2MKwwZqK7c1iopU9HrGFWC4IglZ4ws2yp1FxCN8EQV3ypMnJBS_GdKlLEn3O797yr7slZplaTgRyfsd0-cJ5eTfAtvOL3iYqnc0hL7B6PxJjeOuMJWR2A671qnbBOphZ5x6L0F6Cfnv265PM9qhXOpUmTB93ZmaQ6mNWqMsQDk?purpose=inline)

**A. Living survivor world**

NPCs should have their own daily schedules. They sleep, eat, gather resources, communicate, defend settlements, and respond to zombie attacks even when the player is not directly controlling them.

[They Are Billions Game Customer Remake | Recreate a Playable Game Prototype with AI | SEELE AI](https://images.openai.com/static-rsc-4/X_Cmo2olbVMpuWYJWN_mN49cffmrMx7Z2KWd-PXhAF3BpxYp7ENPV-Ja7usc51aMnN9IILNPFvqv9nkDoD5JbvlCj1UmqdMc--mYyPrCuDkJrIQUzxXNrvPFzL-MIQZOYpjy-jOGFK_CkkUeCg7qe2AVfCkaHCae0ees56buO9Y?purpose=inline)

**B. Intelligent zombie evolution**

Zombies should become more dangerous through environmental and outbreak progression. Introduce rare mutations, stronger hordes, and new boss variants without simply increasing every zombie's health.

[Buy Surviving the Aftermath PC Steam - Strategy - WinGameStore](https://images.openai.com/static-rsc-4/TUbVCKmxqIygUkC4UIVdZt2SwYZvPCMfCN3tH4Zq4ZjYBw1-tkiiOTiLSRv04XBqY7NEUvXlVB8Miypb88P_Ro9CFNjlC7WfmpXdwsBVlQ_CxXebbApQ77RJR7NJePhQlXDjB9xCqz0j-roAxtGA7_Oey4eMYvxQZGfW6AxJ8PI?purpose=inline)

**C. A world that remembers**

If the player abandons a location, the environment should continue changing. Settlements can collapse, resources can disappear, survivors can relocate, and abandoned bases can become zombie territory.

**One important development consideration:** A complete game with this scope is a substantial project. I would build a playable vertical slice first: Day 1, one explorable city district, three playable characters, basic survival, five zombie types, inventory, crafting, and cloud saving. Once those systems work together, expand toward the full 12-character roster, boss ecosystem, and endless world.

That way, you get an actual playable survival game instead of a large collection of unfinished features.